summary:
  The settings pages find a row of their list in the popup's by its address,
  not by its name and uuid.

history:
  The popup moves rows and never renames them. Keyed on the address, an
  older heal's prev took another row's place, a heal onto an address another
  saved row held dropped a station, and of two rows on one address the wrong
  one took the change (measured on the page, 2026-11-02 and 2026-11-03).

target:
  package/contents/ui/ReorderLogic.js

find:
      return String(r.name === undefined ? "" : r.name) + "\u0001" + String(r.uuid === undefined ? "" : r.uuid)

replace:
      return ""

expect:
  Killed by tst_reorderlogic::test_merge_follows_a_heal_onto_an_address_another_row_holds.
  Line-neutral.
